## Codebase onboarding (repo-onboarding skill)

This project has a `repo-onboarding` skill available at `CLONE_PATH/SKILL.md`.

When asked to onboard to this codebase, give an architecture overview, explain how
something works here, or where to make a change, read `CLONE_PATH/SKILL.md` first and
follow its process:

1. Run `CLONE_PATH/scripts/diff-check.sh --from-index .` to see whether a map already
   exists at `.claude/repo-map/` and whether it is stale.
2. On a first run, run `CLONE_PATH/scripts/scan.sh . --format markdown` and synthesize
   `.claude/repo-map/{architecture.md,modules.md,entry-points.md,conventions.md,index.json}`
   as SKILL.md describes.
3. On later runs, re-scan only the directories reported under
   `AFFECTED MODULES / DIRECTORIES` and patch the affected map sections in place.
4. Before making any code-level claim, open and read the actual source files. Cite
   exact `file:line` references, and back any convention claim with 1 to 2 real examples.
